- **Problem in one sentence:** <no technical terms — what is being found out?>
- **Prior threads:** <2–3 [[wikilinks]], each with half a sentence on why
  they lead here>

## Setup

- **Data / scope:** <!-- s --> <source, N, producer script; pilot subset first>
- **Model / tool:** <!-- sm --> <alias from `models.toml` — never hardcode endpoint/ID>
  <two arms (profiles) compared? one line each, held by finalize against the run:
  Arm `before`: register/profiles/<x>.toml @ <fingerprint>, model=<alias>
  Arm `after`: register/profiles/<y>.toml @ <fingerprint>, model=<alias> — and
  the diff between the two profiles verbatim under Prompt>
- **Prompt (verbatim, per variant):** <!-- sm -->

  ```text
  <the real prompt — `protocol-fill PROTOCOL-<name>.md --prompts` writes it from the script's PROMPT constants>
  ```

- **Model I/O:** <in: which fields · out as instructed: required format ·
  out in fact: what comes back + which function parses it>
- **Gate labels (expected) †:** <which labels the gate accepts — the declared
  set for the mechanical check against code-extracted labels>
- **Null condition / anchors (in the same run):** <!-- sm --> <one A per anchor — what runs along in THIS
  run and must show null — anchors of known rate, placebo (safest: one whose
  true answer is the same for every item), swap; not "was
  validated earlier". Per anchor its expected outcome WITH the derivation
  in half a sentence (→ LAB-037 Every anchor carries its target and rationale)>
- **Exclusions / filters:** <!-- s --> <what is dropped from the data or output and why;
  which outputs get no gate label — "none" if nothing is excluded>
- **Unit:** <!-- s --> <what one counted or judged thing is — and what is not:
  hidden files, nested directories, empty cases, a second answer line>
- **Data preparation †:** <raw → prepared: which script wrote which file;
  the experiment reads prepared only>
- **Meaning of the gold label †:** <what does the positive class REALLY
  mean? Check on the rendered example, not on the definition>
- **Answer form + resolution †:** <how many distinguishable states does the
  answer have, and where does the expected value sit?>
- **How measured †:** <metric or mechanism: what is compared, what counted>
- **Validation †:** <anchor items, second model or self-consistency, cross-check>
- **Noise ceiling → threshold †:** <measure repetition spread; the threshold
  comes from the null condition of THIS run>
- **Free knobs †:** <every preprocessing parameter with its value:
  thresholds, filters, cutoffs, windows>
- **Randomness controls †:** <seeds, number of runs, temperature setting
  and why — "deterministic" if no randomness>

## Checks (render check → instrument check → pilot)

- **Resolution check (ZERO calls, real `evaluate()` on synthetic
  extremes):** <perfect effect → criterion fires? · null effect → stays
  silent? Both numbers, with the run's real draw structure — computed by
  the actual evaluation code, never a hand copy of the formula; permanent
  form: `tests/test_<NN>_<name>.py`, run by `preflight` (→ LAB-016 Resolution check before freezing)>
- **Render check (ZERO calls, `--show N`):** <per gold class ONE rendered
  prompt, read verbatim: stacked negation, fields inserted empty, sentences
  the question form cannot decide?>
- **Instrument check (real pipeline, ~10 calls, `--probe N`):** <per gold
  class ONE fully rendered prompt+answer pair as a code block, real data
  (→ LAB-014 One fully rendered example pair per gold class)>
- **Yield per stage:** <expected vs. obtained per parse step (→ LAB-023 No silent loss)>
- **Parser cases harvested:** <the probe's answer forms as REAL cases into
  the parser test — this is where they exist for the first time>
- **Clarified terms:** <what was ambiguous, and what is it called now?>
- **Changed — and in which class:** <instrument (wording, answer form,
  parser, field names) is allowed; hypothesis, criterion, admissibility condition are not
  — changes BEFORE the freeze, from the render and instrument checks
  (→ LAB-008 Instrument check before freezing); what moved after the freeze is
  "Deviations after freeze" under Result>
- **Pilot:** <N items checked against hand analysis or anchors, before scaling>

